WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/system/components/CollapsibleCommandGroup.tsx — a PURE presentational disclosure container:
    <div>
      <ControlButton variant="ghost" size="sm" aria-expanded={open} onClick={toggle}>
          <Icon h-4 w-4 text-muted />
          <span text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-secondary font-medium> t(meta.labelKey, meta.fallback) </span>
          <span text-[10px] text-muted> ({count}) </span>
          <ChevronDown h-3.5 w-3.5 text-muted ml-auto, rotate-180 when open />
      </ControlButton>
      {open && <FadeIn><div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3 mt-2">{children}</div></FadeIn>}
    </div>
  Props: category (web CommandCategory), vehicleId, children, count, defaultOpen=false.
  meta = CATEGORY_META[category] from web/src/features/system/commands.ts (labelKey, fallback, Lucide icon);
         CommandCategory is a 14-value union in the web CATEGORY_ORDER.
  State: a single per-(vehicle,category) open flag mirrored into sessionStorage under
         `teslasync-cat-${vehicleId}-${category}`; seeded via `stored !== null ? stored === 'true' : defaultOpen`.
  Hooks: useTranslation ONLY. No data hooks → NO loading/empty/error/stale/offline data branches
         (those belong to the embedded command tiles, not to this container — same contract as the sibling ToolCard
         surface, whose prompt records "Data sources: (none — pure presentational component)"). The container's
         own branches are: collapsed / expanded(grid) / and an expanded-but-no-commands case.

